\title{The conjunctive property}
\taxon{Module}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\author{reidbarton}
\date{2026-09-15}
\import{stt-macros}

\p{
The \em{conjunctive property} states that for any #{i\,j : \II}, if
#{i \land j = 0}, then #{i = 0} or #{j = 0}. We show that if
\ol{
\li{
The interval is [directed](Synthetic.Directedness): any endomap on #{\II} is
monotone.
}
\li{The booleans cover the crisp elements of #{\II}.}
\li{Types with a terminal object separate.}
}
then #{\II} satisfies the conjunctive property.
}

\p{
The present module is a wrapper that reexports the results from
[[Synthetic.DisjunctiveProperty]] instantiated on the opposite lattice. Note that
these exports don't all judgmentally correspond to the expected results. Directedness
of the opposite lattice is not the same as directedness of the underlying lattice.
This is because inequality is a notion that is derived rather than primitive in our
development of lattices. Likewise, the dual of an initial object is not
judgmentally the same as a terminal object. See \Issue{208} for more details.
}

\agda{
open import Foundations.Universes
open import Algebra.Lattice

module Synthetic.ConjunctiveProperty
  {@♭ 𝓘} (@♭ Δ¹ : Type 𝓘) (@♭ I : Lattice Δ¹)
  where

open import Algebra.Lattice.Instances.Opposite

open import Synthetic.DisjunctiveProperty Δ¹ (Lattice-op I) public
  using ()
  renaming
    ( generating-fam-disjunctive←∨=1-crisp to generating-fam-conjunctive←∧=0-crisp
    ; Λ[2,2]-∨²-incl-♭-section to Λ[2,0]-∧²-incl-♭-section
    ; Λ[2,2]-∨²-incl-is-♭-equiv to Λ[2,0]-∧²-incl-is-♭-equiv
    ; Λ[2,2]-∨²-incl-is-♭-surjective to Λ[2,0]-∧²-incl-is-♭-surjective
    ; generating-fam-disjunctive←Λ[2,2]-∨²-♭-surjective
        to generating-fam-conjunctive←Λ[2,0]-∨²-♭-surjective
    ; generating-fam-disjunctive←∨=1-initial to generating-fam-conjunctive←∧=0-terminal
    ; postcomp-Λ[2,2]-∨²-incl-is-♭-equiv to postcomp-Λ[2,0]-∧²-incl-is-♭-equiv
    ; Λ[2,2]-∨²-incl-is-equiv to Λ[2,0]-∧²-incl-is-equiv
    ; disjunctive-property' to conjunctive-property'
    ; disjunctive-property to conjunctive-property)
}
